{"name":"Mink Frost","hex":"#d7cfc6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any semi-aquatic, carnivorous mammal in the Mustelinae subfamily, similar to weasels, with dark fur, native to Europe and America, of which two species in different genera are extant: the American mink (Neogale vison) and the European mink (Mustela lutreola).","The fur or pelt of a mink, used to make apparel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mink"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mink","blocks":[{"text":"Mink are dark-coloured, semiaquatic, carnivorous mammals in the genera Mustela and Neogale and part of the family Mustelidae, which also includes weasels, stoats, martens, otters, badgers, and others. There are two extant species referred to as \"mink\", the American mink and the European mink. The extinct sea mink was related to the American mink but was much larger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/American_Mink.jpg/330px-American_Mink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mink","wikidata":"Q17700"},{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330px-Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frost","wikidata":"Q4590598"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Europ%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg/500px-Europ%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Europ%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg/500px-Europ%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"European mink (Mustela lutreola)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEurop%C3%A4ischer_Nerz.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg/500px-Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg/1280px-Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg/500px-Mink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mink eating a crayfish","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMink_with_crayfish_at_Wascana_Lake_in_Regina_Saskatchewan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Mink_in_the_snow.png/500px-Mink_in_the_snow.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.